        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1291">

                <pb facs="1011" n="935" xml:id="pg935"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 319.1123L25/44</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 926</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Relating further to the investigation by
                    Panama of the Colon riot of April 2, 1915, I have the honor to enclose copy and
                    translation of a response from the Panaman Foreign Office to my note, which was
                    an enclosure with my despatch No. 922 of May 6, 1916. I shall furnish a copy
                    duly to the Military Commander of the Canal Zone.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Jennings Price</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>







